WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.740
Welcome to 'Ear Biscuits',

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.080
the podcast where two lifelong friends

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.730
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:10.563
I'm Link.

00:00:10.563 --> 00:00:11.396
And I'm Rhett.

00:00:11.396 --> 00:00:13.800
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.530
we are continuing what is
now the annual tradition.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:20.550
This would be the third annual?

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:21.590
Yeah--

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.050
How do you do anniversaries like that?

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:24.140
It's the third time.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.040
The third time?

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:26.373
The second update.

00:00:28.137 --> 00:00:29.480
Let's say it's the third anniversary.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.480
The third anniversary of our going public

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.510
with our deconstruction stories.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.570
Well, it was two years ago.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.360
So that's the two year anniversary.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.390
Two year.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.920
See, the numbers confuse me,

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.710
and I know they confuse you.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.543
What?

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:45.950
These engineering degrees, man.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.290
We're only talking about
the numbers two or three.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.290
So, come on,

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.650
let's pull this together.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.050
Two years ago,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:57.050
we talked about all of our spirituality

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:59.610
leading up to the present day,

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:03.120
including our spiritual deconstruction

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.540
from the white Evangelical Church,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.000
to be very specific about it.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.370
A lot of people,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.770
because we talk about it as a, you know,

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:15.740
our deconstruction
anniversary or whatever.

00:01:15.740 --> 00:01:17.350
That's not technically true,

00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:19.980
because some people think, oh,

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.573
so two years ago, when
you guys told your story,

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:24.620
that was when you deconstructed.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.500
No.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.950
I mean, as I've said many times,

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:30.593
my deconstruction happened
about 10 years ago for me.

00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:32.750
And, you know,

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.927
I stopped calling myself
a Christian in 2013-ish,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.960
so that's getting close to a decade

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.433
of not being a Christian.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.490
But it took us a long time to gain

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.577
the nerve to actually share that.

00:01:49.577 --> 00:01:51.350
And it happened two years ago.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.840
If you didn't listen to those,

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.050
or if you want a refresher of it,

00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.170
that series is called 'The Lost Years'.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.130
It was four or five episodes.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.650
You shared your story, I shared my story.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:06.170
We also shared all of our,

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.420
you know, our spiritual
backgrounds growing up,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.940
our involvement in Campus Crusade

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:11.580
for Christ as college students,

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.210
our involvement as staff members

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.530
working full time with crew.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:20.490
And then we called it 'The Lost Years',

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.213
because that was the part of
our career development that we,

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:28.443
up until that point,

00:02:28.443 --> 00:02:30.690
we had not talked about publicly,

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:33.783
which led into talking about
our spiritual deconstruction.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:35.966
Yeah, you know the word.

00:02:35.966 --> 00:02:37.650
Deconstruction.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.630
And then last year, and yeah,

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.870
so that was right before the pandemic hit,

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.380
and then it just kind of seemed like

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.750
a year later we gave an update.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.197
So we're gonna do that.

00:02:47.197 --> 00:02:48.970
You know, that doesn't mean we only

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:50.400
talk about spiritual things once a year,

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.560
but each year we want to give each of us

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:55.600
an opportunity to sort of say,

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.530
hey, this is where I'm at.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.930
This is how I'm continuing to process,

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:03.250
because the process of
what's happening in our

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:05.240
spiritual lives is something that unfolds.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:09.820
And this is like the
definitive update for me.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:10.960
We're gonna start with me,

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.268
and next week we'll do Link's.

00:03:14.268 --> 00:03:16.480
Yeah, and I'm looking forward to this,

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.953
because, I mean,

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.140
we see each other so often,

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:24.010
and we're having so many conversations,

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.180
and we're, you know,

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.380
we have so many,

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:29.210
so many things come
through our lives that,

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:30.710
first of all, make its way onto the show,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.760
but second of all, don't.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:34.940
They're more private
that we still talk about.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.410
Some of those things
are spiritual in nature,

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:42.400
but there always seems to
be really pressing matters,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.340
and then just your life
kind of gets away from you.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:47.300
So it's like we don't sit
down and talk for an hour,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.350
an hour and a half.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.183
It's like, hey,

00:03:49.183 --> 00:03:52.280
so give me your spiritual update.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:53.113
You know?

00:03:53.113 --> 00:03:55.500
It just kind of comes
out in bits and pieces.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.280
So I'm looking forward to hearing

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:59.403
more of this bonafide update.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.590
And I was about to say,

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:04.390
and I'm also looking
forward to giving mine,

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.680
but I'm honestly not.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.691
So we'll see what
happens a week from now--

00:04:07.691 --> 00:04:09.230
Let's get started, 'cause
as you might imagine,

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:10.493
I've got quite a lot to say.

00:04:10.493 --> 00:04:11.326
Yeah.

00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:12.159
I'm all ears, man.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.800
I'm always,

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.710
I approach these, the first
one and the second one,

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.543
and now the third one,

00:04:18.543 --> 00:04:21.610
I approach these with the
certain amount of trepidation,

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.883
because what I have found
is many of the things

00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:28.430
that I say during these
podcasts are then...

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.263
Sound bited?

00:04:29.263 --> 00:04:31.840
Sound bited across the internet,

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.560
through multiple platforms,

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.100
for people, with people,

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.210
or by people who agree with me,

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.960
and people who don't agree with me.

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.420
And so as I calculate,

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.950
I end up writing down quite
a lot that I want to get to

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.410
because I'm trying to
calculate what I'm gonna say,

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.920
because it will either be used against me,

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.120
or it will be, you know.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.000
It is what it is, but I'm
just letting you know.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.330
I don't necessarily look
forward to this either,

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:58.690
because these episodes,

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:01.230
there's a level of scrutiny
that is applied to them

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.000
that I'm not exactly
interested in inviting.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.760
But it is what it is, and it's now,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:09.150
it's just happening annually, I guess.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:09.983
Yeah.

00:05:09.983 --> 00:05:14.210
There's a heightened awareness
of people listening in,

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.463
and different groups
of people listening in.

00:05:15.463 --> 00:05:17.760
It's not just you talking to me,

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:19.860
where we can get lost in that conversation

00:05:20.907 --> 00:05:23.136
on a normal 'Ear Biscuit'.

00:05:23.136 --> 00:05:24.063
Which you can't--

00:05:24.063 --> 00:05:25.696
And also, you know,

00:05:25.696 --> 00:05:27.300
there's this weird balance with

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.640
these things are very personal,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.160
but yet we have a public platform

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:35.800
where we share personal things that we,

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.493
you know, we've never really,

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.750
we've talked about that
and thought about that,

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:45.430
but there's a weirdness to that.

00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:46.760
There's a weirdness to this like, okay,

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:47.930
I'm experiencing these things,

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:50.410
and I'm in process, and I'm not,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.460
I haven't come to all these

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.210
definitive conclusions or anything,

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.330
but I'm sharing them,

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.920
and I'm putting them out into the world.

00:05:56.920 --> 00:05:59.090
And then they are used by other

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.980
people to either form conclusions,

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:02.203
make conclusions,

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.200
to combat other people's ideas,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:10.220
defend ideas that maybe I
didn't even want to be defended.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.950
It's just a weird, there's a
weird dynamic to doing this.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:16.400
But let's not spend too
much talking about that,

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.650
'cause I do have quite a
bit that has happened--

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:21.030
But there is a positive side too, right?

00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:21.980
I mean, there's a reason that you're

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.820
ultimately deciding to still do it.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.653
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:25.653 --> 00:06:26.486
Oh yeah.

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:31.486
I think that the response
that we have gotten

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:34.140
anytime we've been vulnerable
about these spiritual things

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:36.530
has been so encouraging because this is

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.890
a deeply personal thing
to millions and millions,

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:41.450
billions, most people on the Earth,

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:43.740
and most people in the
history of the world

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:46.440
have had some sort of religious conviction

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.730
that probably changed over time.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.870
And so when people talk about what

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.130
their religious convictions are,

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:53.460
there sort of spiritual perspective

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:54.980
and how it's changed over time,

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:56.350
I think there's just a,

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:58.110
it's part of the human experience.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:02.820
And I know for a fact that
our story resonates with a lot

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.850
of people who have come from
a very similar background,

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.450
have experienced similar things.

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:10.840
But again, I don't do this.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.200
I try not to do this.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.710
My natural disposition
is to try to persuade,

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.150
and try to convince.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:19.050
I have an Evangelistic personality.

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:21.770
I don't like that about
myself necessarily.

00:07:21.770 --> 00:07:24.190
That's something I'm
actively trying to change

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.550
so that I can kind of get out

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:30.993
of the convincing business as I get older.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.160
So this is more of, hey,

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:36.400
this is what's going on with me.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.023
Do with it what you will.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:40.800
Right.

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:41.633
Shoulder shrug.

00:07:41.633 --> 00:07:43.090
Okay, so,

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:46.190
at the end of last year, the end of 2021,

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.630
I actually told my wife.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.463
I said,

00:07:49.722 --> 00:07:51.310
you know,

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:53.403
I kind of feel like I'm just,

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:57.790
I don't have a huge appetite
for spiritual things right now.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.441
Like I just don't,

00:07:59.441 --> 00:08:01.713
maybe that's just not gonna be me.

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:06.800
Fast forward to the
beginning of this year,

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:09.913
so literally just a few weeks ago,

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:14.318
and I'm ordering a Bible on Amazon.

00:08:14.318 --> 00:08:15.498
Okay.
So, just.

00:08:17.046 --> 00:08:18.010
Okay.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.380
Just to give you a little preview.

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:21.213
Not that I didn't have a Bible--

00:08:21.213 --> 00:08:22.410
The Amazon Bible.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:27.040
Is it Jeff Bezos red line edition?

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.147
What's the Amazon, what's the--

00:08:28.147 --> 00:08:29.017
The Ben Franklin Bible.

00:08:29.017 --> 00:08:32.009
What's the Amazon brand for batteries?

00:08:32.009 --> 00:08:33.373
I don't know.

00:08:33.373 --> 00:08:35.797
What do you call the
batteries that you can get--

00:08:35.797 --> 00:08:37.476
I would say Kirkland,
that's the Walmart version.

00:08:37.476 --> 00:08:39.105
You don't get the Amazon batteries?

00:08:39.105 --> 00:08:40.078
Amazon Basics?

00:08:40.078 --> 00:08:42.289
Yeah, I got the Amazon Basics Bible.

00:08:42.289 --> 00:08:45.110
No you didn't.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:48.058
No, you'll understand why I got a Bible.

00:08:48.058 --> 00:08:49.720
I already had plenty of Bibles,

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:51.100
but why I got a specific Bible.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:52.120
Okay.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:53.960
Just a little tease, just a little tease.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.240
So how did I get here?

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.930
Okay, so since deconstructing,

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.340
and really deconverting, you know?

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:05.320
I didn't just deconstruct, I deconverted,

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.720
I'm not a Christian anymore,

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.200
which has been almost a decade for me.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.070
I have dabbled in a lot of
spiritual things, right?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.763
Spiritual in quotes.

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:17.870
But that kind,

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:21.203
that has all kind of happened
outside of any sort of system.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:23.798
You know, I haven't,

00:09:23.798 --> 00:09:24.733
I didn't like, oh,

00:09:24.733 --> 00:09:26.940
I wanna see what Buddhism feels like,

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.920
like officially, you know?

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.880
I've read a lot of interesting stuff,

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.000
and I've read a lot of spiritual writers.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:36.470
I've been really attracted to people

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:38.240
who kind of take Western and Eastern

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:40.420
philosophies and kind of bridge them,

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:41.390
bring them together.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.190
People like Eckhart Tolle.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.830
I've been very encouraged,

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:48.420
and there's been some
realizations that I've had

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.603
while reading spiritual writers.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:54.500
I'm not gonna go into
what all that has been,

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.690
but it's been significant,

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:00.450
and it has been characterized more

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:03.550
as realization rather than revelation.

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:04.383
Right?

00:10:04.383 --> 00:10:06.220
So I make that distinction that these

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:08.040
are more realizations than revelations,

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.300
because revelation is
something that feels like

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.610
you're getting something
from somewhere else.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.790
Like you're literally getting

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.980
something revealed to you by God.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:19.520
You know, it hasn't been
anything on that level.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:20.780
It's more like epiphanies.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:21.790
Like, oh,

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:23.340
never thought about that.

00:10:23.340 --> 00:10:25.840
But that applies to something
that I can only apply,

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:27.610
only describe as spirituality.

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:29.833
I know that's pretty amorphous, but.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.070
But I have stopped short of going

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:36.950
too deep into anything, right?

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:41.950
Because the more structured and systematic

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:46.770
a spiritual system gets,

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.173
the more suspect I become of it, right?

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.580
So take, for instance,

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:54.100
you know, we live in Los Angeles.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:55.900
So we're in Southern California,

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.670
where if there is a
religion of this region,

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.503
it is New Ageism in general, right?

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.873
People who buy crystals because they think

00:11:04.873 --> 00:11:06.900
that the crystals have specific

00:11:06.900 --> 00:11:08.530
spiritual powers or whatever,

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.000
and bring certain, you know,

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:14.210
there's literally a metaphysical
power to these crystals.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:17.230
Like you leave it in the moonlight
to charge it with energy,

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.410
right?

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:21.900
Lots of people, as you can
imagine here on the West Coast,

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:22.733
believe this.

00:11:22.733 --> 00:11:25.580
You Might trip on a curb
and land in a crystal shop.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.413
Yeah.

00:11:26.413 --> 00:11:29.000
Now I don't believe that is true.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:29.860
Like I, you know,

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:31.350
it might be,

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:36.350
but in many ways it begins
to resemble the same sort of

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.500
metaphysical convictions
about things that you can't

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:43.100
really be sure about that I ran away from

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.120
when it comes to
Fundamentalist Christianity,

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:46.600
or Conservative Christianity.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:47.490
Yeah.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.450
And so I'm just really suspect of systems.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:52.170
So I'm not about to become like, hey,

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:53.270
I'm the new age guy,

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.040
and I've got this crystal around my neck

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.390
that's giving me this spirit of clarity.

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:02.760
Again, I'm not saying
definitively that that's not true,

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:07.720
because what I am saying is
that I can't believe that.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:08.553
You know?

00:12:08.553 --> 00:12:11.400
I am incapable of believing that,

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:13.830
because there's something
about me that makes me

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.300
incapable of buying into something

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.483
that it feels like you've
taken a bridge too far.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.480
You got up to a certain place,

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:25.570
you followed rationality and
logic it to a certain place,

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:28.040
and then you had to make a big jump

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:29.910
into some metaphysical reality.

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:30.990
And when you make that jump,

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:32.930
I'm kind of like, cool!

00:12:32.930 --> 00:12:34.140
If that's good for you, that's great.

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.220
But I don't believe I
can go there with you,

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.430
because there's just something built

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:39.500
into me that causes me to,

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:40.640
I get up against this wall,

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:41.473
and I'm like, I can't go there.

00:12:41.473 --> 00:12:43.350
Even if it seems fun, I can't do that.

00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:44.203
I can't go there.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:46.803
But the interesting thing--

00:12:46.803 --> 00:12:47.660
You thought you might,

00:12:48.511 --> 00:12:50.211
but you determined that you can't.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.400
Well, I kinda,

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:58.400
I've been very wary of
leaving one religious system.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.470
I didn't think that the next stage

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.880
was joining another religious system.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:03.713
Yeah.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:10.760
But the interesting thing is
that my search for purpose,

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:14.790
meaning, has never waned in the process.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:18.280
So even though I became very unsure

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.590
about what my world view is,

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:22.270
in terms of how I think
about spiritual things,

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:23.717
and whether or not God exists,

00:13:23.717 --> 00:13:27.070
and if God does exist,
what is the nature of God?

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:30.400
What is the nature of God's
interaction with me as a person?

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.740
How real can it be?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:34.920
How substantial can it be?

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:37.833
Substantive I think is the
word I was looking for.

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:42.020
I have never,

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.610
I feel like I can't draw
conclusions about those things,

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.403
but I haven't lost,

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:48.820
I didn't say,

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:51.593
and none of it matters, and
I'm not interested in it.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:55.640
What I realized is that
there is what I would call

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:58.953
a religious disposition in my
personality at the same time.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:02.400
So this is, you know,

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:03.623
so talking about that,

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.623
my desire for purpose and
meaning never really waning.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:11.230
That's why I was such a serious

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.400
Christian to begin with, right?

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:17.263
That's why, and I think I
speak for you in this as well.

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:22.040
That's why I was really all
about my faith in high school

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.150
when my friends started
being all about partying,

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.537
and sex, and everything else,

00:14:25.537 --> 00:14:26.950
the stuff I was thinking about,

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.870
but I was really like, no man.

00:14:29.870 --> 00:14:31.040
If this is true,

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:35.780
if it is true that Jesus
is the connection to God,

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:39.500
Jesus is God, and there is a
spiritual reality that exists.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.410
If that is true,

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:44.224
that's way more important
than Friday night!

00:14:44.224 --> 00:14:45.320
You know?

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:47.650
That's way more important
than having a good time.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.532
And so my life has been,

00:14:50.532 --> 00:14:53.910
my religious life when I
was spiritually a Christian,

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.373
and a current Conservative Christian,

00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:58.773
you know,

00:14:58.773 --> 00:15:00.960
I took it very, very seriously.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.410
And it's why college was characterized

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:06.060
by just being involved
in a campus ministry,

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:07.500
and basically my entire social life

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.530
and all my activities
being centered around that,

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:12.070
going on staff with Campus Crusade

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.130
with you after we graduated,

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.500
basically becoming missionaries,

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:19.330
training people to share
Jesus throughout the world,

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:23.020
because it was the most
important thing that there was.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:23.853
Yeah.

00:15:23.853 --> 00:15:26.520
You know, it was a very simple,

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:30.410
logical argument that
resonated with both of us.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:34.200
And I think I'll end up talking about,

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.240
I know I'll end up talking
about my story next week,

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.480
so I'm not gonna do that here,

00:15:37.480 --> 00:15:42.480
but just exploring the why for me has,

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:45.360
starting to do that has been enlightening.

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.050
You know, I think it's,

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:50.730
yes, it resonates with my personality

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:53.810
and your personality in different ways,

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:58.810
but to a similar result
of being very fervent,

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:00.830
almost being like a zealot.

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:02.530
We were like high school zealots.

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:03.700
Yeah.

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.393
It was also something that was very,

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:11.890
indoctrinated is an aggressive word,

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.910
but we were strongly educated in these.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:17.340
It was drilled into us, you know?

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:18.343
So I wonder, like,

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:22.950
do you understand what it
is about yourself that,

00:16:22.950 --> 00:16:25.610
like even now with more distance,

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:28.960
that made you latch onto it?

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.110
'Cause I don't know if it's the same

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:31.683
reasons for you as for me.

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:33.983
I don't know.

00:16:33.983 --> 00:16:34.816
I don't know.

00:16:34.816 --> 00:16:36.577
And I'm not--

00:16:36.577 --> 00:16:39.370
But when it comes to ideas
and it comes to, like,

00:16:39.370 --> 00:16:41.660
right and wrong is something that

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.580
very much resonated with both of us.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:45.260
I just don't know if for the same reasons.

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:46.830
I think that the,

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:48.047
again, I may be deceiving--

00:16:48.047 --> 00:16:49.200
And being right!

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:51.100
I may be deceiving myself,

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:52.800
but the thing that I have always

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:57.640
thought is that whatever is true,

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.633
no matter how uncomfortable it is,

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.870
I've had this inescapable draw to it,

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:05.760
meaning that--

00:17:05.760 --> 00:17:09.980
It's the principle by which you've

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:12.000
had this instinctual draw to it,

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.370
but you've also had this
logical assertion that,

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.460
like, this is the principle
that I'm living by.

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:20.677
This is the highest principle to live by.

00:17:20.677 --> 00:17:22.020
And we definitely.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:26.560
For whatever reason, something being true.

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:28.710
Whether or not it's true makes all

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:30.640
the difference in the world to me, right?

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.730
Again, I'm not saying I'm some perfect,

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:33.670
rational being.

00:17:33.670 --> 00:17:36.700
I'm a product of my
environment, my circumstances,

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:38.600
and my genetics, just like anybody else.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.000
But for whatever reason,

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:43.090
that combination of factors
has led to a place where,

00:17:43.090 --> 00:17:45.380
if something ends up not being true,

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:46.960
it becomes very difficult for me

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:49.290
to believe for convenient reasons.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:50.600
But it also puts you on a,

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.780
it sets up a moral high ground that's,

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:56.190
like, could potentially
be a superiority thing.

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.370
It's like, I know we both took

00:17:57.370 --> 00:18:01.303
pride in where we're coming from.

00:18:02.390 --> 00:18:03.290
Keep going though.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:07.573
So I've retained this
religious disposition.

00:18:08.786 --> 00:18:10.493
I retained this,

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:12.980
for a lack of a better word,

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.320
skepticism, right?

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.770
And in fact, that skepticism,

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:19.399
that was like, if this is,

00:18:19.399 --> 00:18:23.050
you know, what is true is
the most important thing.

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:25.660
It's ultimately how
seriously I took my faith

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:28.253
is the reason for me that I deconstructed.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:32.300
Because I kept going
back to the foundations,

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:33.160
and I kept going back and being like,

00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:34.060
okay, I'm really,

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.800
I'm putting everything out.

00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:37.930
I'm leveraging so much on this.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.310
So much is rooted in this.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.300
If this is not true?

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.170
So I would go back and I
would try to make it true,

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:44.260
and if I was introduced to new information

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:45.490
that seemed like it couldn't fit,

00:18:45.490 --> 00:18:47.770
I would find a way for it to fit,

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:49.310
or I would find a way to push it away.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.930
And it was just constant battle of

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.870
reorganizing and rearranging my faith.

00:18:53.870 --> 00:18:56.570
Relaying that foundation,
making sure the foundation.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.060
I was constantly inspecting
the building of my faith,

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:00.893
and being like, oh,

00:19:00.893 --> 00:19:02.406
there's a little crack there.

00:19:02.406 --> 00:19:05.110
Let's replace those bricks, whatever.

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.700
And then of course you know the story,

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.780
I've already told that story.

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:10.930
I got to a place where I could not,

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.200
the foundation itself was made out

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:15.400
of the wrong material is what I thought,

00:19:15.400 --> 00:19:17.610
and I basically demolished
the whole building.

00:19:17.610 --> 00:19:18.930
I deconstructed.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.810
That's where the whole
idea comes from, right?

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:22.960
You're tearing it down.

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:28.400
But I've realized that there's
been these two parallel,

00:19:28.400 --> 00:19:32.170
seemingly conflicting forces in my

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:33.810
life for a really long time,

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:38.720
and that is my relentless skepticism,

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.290
and then my persistent
desire for ultimate meaning.

00:19:42.290 --> 00:19:47.053
Those two things just
refuse to die, right?

00:19:48.385 --> 00:19:51.820
And so, you know,

00:19:51.820 --> 00:19:54.920
they've been in my personality in kind of

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.950
relative conflict for a long time,

00:19:57.950 --> 00:20:00.820
but I think the, I'll call it an epiphany.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:02.040
That's probably too strong of a word,

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.160
but I'll call an epiphany.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:04.640
The thing that I've realized.

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:06.558
You can call it an etiphany.

00:20:06.558 --> 00:20:11.050
This year is that, it's
just asking the question.

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.910
What if I don't deny either my

00:20:12.910 --> 00:20:15.203
skepticism or my spirituality?

00:20:15.203 --> 00:20:17.380
So simplifying those terms.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:20.530
What if they can inform
and enhance one another?

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:23.100
So that,

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:25.610
as I look at 2022,

00:20:25.610 --> 00:20:26.580
you know, one year at a time,

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.090
one step at a time.

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.800
That is the thing that I'm focusing on.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:34.440
So that seems like, what
do you mean by that?

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:36.063
So let me try to explain it.

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:40.010
So one of the things that I've done

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:43.080
in trying to figure out
how these two things

00:20:43.080 --> 00:20:44.820
meet in me and inform one another,

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:46.370
the skepticism and the spirituality,

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:47.900
is looking for people who I think

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.810
are kind of writing that line.

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.330
Looking for other people out there

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.500
who seem to embrace both
of both of these things.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.450
Right?

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:55.860
So one person that I found,

00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:57.770
and I can't remember how I found

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:01.274
all the stuff I'm gonna talk about.

00:21:01.274 --> 00:21:02.107
So be it.

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:06.660
But one person is Maria Popova,

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.460
who runs the website The Marginalian,

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.260
which was formally called Brain Pickings.

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:13.260
She changed the name because, I mean,

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:14.500
I guess brain pickings?

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:15.333
Sounds gross.

00:21:15.333 --> 00:21:18.100
Yeah, I think she finally realized that.

00:21:18.100 --> 00:21:19.080
Marginalia?

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.400
Marginalian, The Marginalian.

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:24.390
I wasn't familiar with this term,

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:27.010
but marginalia is, like,

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:28.580
you've got a book, and there's margins,

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:30.530
and it's the stuff, it's the process,

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.960
it's the writing, it's the notes,

00:21:31.960 --> 00:21:32.793
right?

00:21:32.793 --> 00:21:33.626
That's marginalia.

00:21:33.626 --> 00:21:36.370
It's stuff that is peripheral to

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:37.570
the stuff that you're reading,

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:39.127
and then kind of the
connection between you

00:21:39.127 --> 00:21:40.970
and the material that
you're experiencing, right?

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:43.200
You know people who write a
lot of stuff in the margin.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.620
Yeah.

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:46.420
I usually just make notes on my computer.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:47.253
Huh!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:49.533
Marginalia.

00:21:49.533 --> 00:21:52.460
And let me explain how
she describes her work

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:54.460
so you can kind of get a picture of her.

00:21:55.540 --> 00:21:58.930
She is exploring what it
means to live a decent,

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:03.930
inspired, substantive life
of purpose and gladness.

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:06.100
And, this is from her website,

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:09.190
Marginalia is a record of
my own becoming as person,

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:10.560
intellectually, creatively,

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:12.100
spiritually, poetically,

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:14.050
drawn from my extended marginalia on

00:22:14.050 --> 00:22:15.680
the search for meaning across literature,

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:16.513
science, art,

00:22:16.513 --> 00:22:17.346
philosophy,

00:22:17.346 --> 00:22:20.420
and the various other tendrils
of human thought and feeling.

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:21.580
A private inquiry.

00:22:21.580 --> 00:22:23.890
I can't say that word, inquiry.

00:22:23.890 --> 00:22:24.780
Inquiry?

00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:27.620
I can't say substantive or inquiry,

00:22:27.620 --> 00:22:30.860
and she uses both of them in
a very short span of time.

00:22:30.860 --> 00:22:35.040
A private inquiry irradiated
by the ultimate question,

00:22:35.040 --> 00:22:38.090
the great quickening of
wonderment that binds us all.

00:22:38.090 --> 00:22:40.433
What is all this?

00:22:41.600 --> 00:22:42.433
Okay.

00:22:42.433 --> 00:22:43.750
That is some beautiful language.

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:44.840
First of all, she's a great writer.

00:22:44.840 --> 00:22:45.673
I love her.

00:22:45.673 --> 00:22:48.240
So it's kind of a fun,

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:50.783
it's heady, but it's openhearted.

00:22:52.497 --> 00:22:53.414
It's a...

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:55.560
It's not critical.

00:22:55.560 --> 00:22:56.800
In her inner,

00:22:56.800 --> 00:22:58.773
mm, it is critical.

00:23:00.110 --> 00:23:02.890
It is critical, but it's not closed.

00:23:02.890 --> 00:23:04.230
Okay.
Okay?

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:07.523
So in her interview with
Terry Gross on being,

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:12.673
she talked about the bridge
between cynicism and hope,

00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:16.550
and I felt like that's it.

00:23:16.550 --> 00:23:19.820
This bridge has slowly
been constructing itself.

00:23:19.820 --> 00:23:22.260
Maybe it's always been there in me

