00:35:07.140 --> 00:35:08.650
and Moses probably didn't exist.

00:35:08.650 --> 00:35:10.880
But setting that aside for a second,

00:35:10.880 --> 00:35:15.880
it was the idea that it was
written in a certain time,

00:35:17.640 --> 00:35:21.090
but it was written about the past.

00:35:21.090 --> 00:35:22.880
It was writing about the past,

00:35:22.880 --> 00:35:24.200
but it was really also writing about

00:35:24.200 --> 00:35:26.680
what they were currently experiencing.

00:35:26.680 --> 00:35:27.513
Right?

00:35:27.513 --> 00:35:28.346
So looking,

00:35:28.346 --> 00:35:30.510
he talks about the story of Daniel

00:35:30.510 --> 00:35:32.140
and how it related to what the Jews

00:35:32.140 --> 00:35:35.670
were going through at the
time under Roman rule,

00:35:35.670 --> 00:35:37.080
wasn't necessarily so much about

00:35:37.080 --> 00:35:39.683
what was happening in Daniel's time.

00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:45.477
Okay, so more as a parable
written as history.

00:35:45.477 --> 00:35:47.450
And then even he talks about,

00:35:47.450 --> 00:35:48.630
you know, he talks about
the creation story,

00:35:48.630 --> 00:35:51.460
but he also talks about
Jesus himself, right?

00:35:51.460 --> 00:35:53.540
Which again, we don't really know.

00:35:53.540 --> 00:35:55.420
We don't actually know definitively

00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:57.730
too much about the
historical figure of Jesus,

00:35:57.730 --> 00:35:59.570
or some people believe
he didn't even exist.

00:35:59.570 --> 00:36:00.990
I think he did exist,

00:36:00.990 --> 00:36:02.310
but I think that the Jesus that we have

00:36:02.310 --> 00:36:07.310
in the Bible is a sort of idealized figure

00:36:07.540 --> 00:36:11.400
that was a story that was told,

00:36:11.400 --> 00:36:14.130
because it was the story that the people

00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:16.380
who were telling it needed at the time.

00:36:16.380 --> 00:36:17.213
Right?

00:36:17.213 --> 00:36:19.993
And this is true of
every religious writing.

00:36:22.060 --> 00:36:23.770
Everything that we,

00:36:23.770 --> 00:36:26.460
every story we tell ourselves, right?

00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:28.520
And so he looks at the
Bible, which is like,

00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.876
