the tendency for people

01:07:41.730 --> 01:07:45.810
to move from one fundamentalism
to another fundamentalism.

01:07:45.810 --> 01:07:48.170
Very, very common in deconstructing,

01:07:48.170 --> 01:07:49.730
is that you leave sort of a

01:07:49.730 --> 01:07:51.700
fundamentalist Christian mindset,

01:07:51.700 --> 01:07:54.850
and you move into a
progressive Christian mindset.

01:07:54.850 --> 01:07:57.850
And a lot of times the
progressive Christian mindset,

01:07:57.850 --> 01:07:59.450
and the progressive left in general

01:07:59.450 --> 01:08:01.850
can have the same sort of inflexible

01:08:01.850 --> 01:08:06.670
fundamentalist thinking
that you have on the right.

01:08:06.670 --> 01:08:07.970
I completely agree with that!

01:08:07.970 --> 01:08:09.670
I don't like ideological thinking.

01:08:09.670 --> 01:08:10.690
I don't like group think.

01:08:10.690 --> 01:08:13.177
I don't like policing the way
people think about things,

01:08:13.177 --> 01:08:14.920
and the way people talk about things,

01:08:14.920 --> 01:08:16.990
and you see that on the left just as

01:08:16.990 --> 01:08:19.390
much as you see it on the right.

01:08:19.390 --> 01:08:21.160
I will say, this entire thing,

01:08:21.160 --> 01:08:24.600
I believe, is written to people
who are not deconstructing.

01:08:24.600 --> 01:08:28.810
It is written to give to people
who you are afraid might,

01:08:28.810 --> 01:08:31.330
to bolster them against ever

01:08:31.330 --> 01:08:34.230
considering spiritual deconstruction.

01:08:34.230 --> 01:08:36.220
It bolsters that.

01:08:36.220 --> 01:08:37.163
I mean, yeah.

01:08:38.428 --> 01:08:41.378
It's for people who haven't
gone over the edge yet, really.

01:08:42.297 --> 01:08:44.900
There's one about race, which talks about,

01:08:44.900 --> 01:08:46.990
yes, acknowledges racism in the Church,

01:08:46.990 --> 01:08:47.823
but says,
hey, listen.

01:08:47.823 --> 01:08:49.930
Just because people
have abused and misused

01:08:49.930 --> 01:08:52.710
Christianity in the
name of evil and racism

01:08:52.710 --> 01:08:54.860
doesn't mean that you should deconstruct.

01:08:54.860 --> 01:08:56.570
I agree with all that.

01:08:56.570 --> 01:08:57.403
But the one thing--

01:08:57.403 --> 01:08:58.821
Heading people off of the pass.

01:08:58.821 --> 01:09:02.800
It also talks about how,
scientism is the word they use,

01:09:02.800 --> 01:09:05.813
but basically science
can't explain morality,

01:09:06.810 --> 01:09:07.790
which I think that, you know,

01:09:07.790 --> 01:09:10.010
there's great natural
explanations for morality

01:09:10.010 --> 01:09:11.160
that they kind of just gloss over.

01:09:11.160 --> 01:09:12.860
But anyway.

01:09:12.860 --> 01:09:14.830
I agree with some, I disagree with some.

01:09:14.830 --> 01:09:17.630
Obviously I disagree a main
conclusion of the book,

01:09:17.630 --> 01:09:19.160
but the thing I wanted to talk about,

01:09:19.160 --> 01:09:20.910
and then bring it back to how it relates

01:09:20.910 --> 01:09:24.253
to kind of how I'm moving forward in 2022,

01:09:25.470 --> 01:09:26.823
is the first chapter,

01:09:28.660 --> 01:09:30.390
which is written by a guy named--

01:09:30.390 --> 01:09:31.504
Trevin Wax.
Trevin Wax,

01:09:31.504 --> 01:09:32.702
there are names.

01:09:32.702 --> 01:09:33.800
Doubt your way back to truth.

01:09:33.800 --> 01:09:34.713
Ivan Mesa and Trevin Wax.

01:09:34.713 --> 01:09:36.140
They've got cool names.

01:09:36.140 --> 01:09:37.530
This is coming from two
guys with cool names,

01:09:37.530 --> 01:09:38.913
so congrats for that.

01:09:40.260 --> 01:09:41.950
I will cite chapter three.

01:09:41.950 --> 01:09:45.220
Deconversion is not as
counter cultural as you think.

01:09:45.220 --> 01:09:47.290
So, hey,

01:09:47.290 --> 01:09:48.750
this isn't the cool thing to do.

01:09:48.750 --> 01:09:50.720
Yeah, which I agree.

01:09:50.720 --> 01:09:51.630
I agree with that.

01:09:51.630 --> 01:09:52.700
Yeah, don't.

01:09:52.700 --> 01:09:54.260
Don't do it 'cause it's cool.

01:09:54.260 --> 01:09:55.573
Don't do it for those reasons.

01:09:58.030 --> 01:09:59.800
In the first chapter,

01:09:59.800 --> 01:10:01.720
deconstruction is characterized

01:10:01.720 --> 01:10:05.050
as essentially a selfish act, right?

01:10:05.050 --> 01:10:07.797
Rather than a thoughtful
reconsideration of one's faith.

01:10:07.797 --> 01:10:09.799
Let me just, I'm gonna read some quotes.

01:10:09.799 --> 01:10:11.300
I'll just put the book down,

01:10:11.300 --> 01:10:13.003
'cause I've written them down here.

01:10:14.740 --> 01:10:16.570
What if you are not the dispassionate

01:10:16.570 --> 01:10:18.890
pursuer of facts you
perceived yourself to be,

01:10:18.890 --> 01:10:20.810
but instead are shaped by assumptions

01:10:20.810 --> 01:10:23.260
and presuppositions that
you've never challenged.

01:10:24.420 --> 01:10:25.830
Another quote.

01:10:25.830 --> 01:10:27.280
I don't believe you are faithless.

01:10:27.280 --> 01:10:30.670
Your faith has merely shifted
away from God and his word,

01:10:30.670 --> 01:10:33.740
and towards yourself and
the story you've crafted,

01:10:33.740 --> 01:10:36.730
in which you now find
meaning in significance,

01:10:36.730 --> 01:10:38.270
or which you've crafted in which

01:10:38.270 --> 01:10:40.540
you now find meaning in significance.

01:10:40.540 --> 01:10:41.373
And finally,

01:10:41.373 --> 01:10:45.600
you are no longer sure about
the God of Christianity.

01:10:45.600 --> 01:10:47.850
Are you sure of the self you place

01:10:47.850 --> 01:10:49.973
at the center of your deconversion story?

01:10:51.850 --> 01:10:56.417
This is a very common way of seeing

01:10:57.280 --> 01:10:58.980
people who are deconstructing.

01:10:58.980 --> 01:11:00.930
This is how I saw people
who were deconstructing

01:11:00.930 --> 01:11:02.090
before I could deconstruct it.

01:11:02.090 --> 01:11:05.020
When we had friends who started to waiver,

01:11:05.020 --> 01:11:06.563
we would say, listen man,

01:11:07.630 --> 01:11:09.300
you're making God in your own image

01:11:09.300 --> 01:11:11.367
rather than realizing that
you're made in his image.

01:11:11.367 --> 01:11:14.730
You're picking and choosing,
you're making a religion,

01:11:14.730 --> 01:11:16.790
you're becoming your own God.

01:11:16.790 --> 01:11:19.909
And that's what deconstruction
ultimately is, right?

01:11:19.909 --> 01:11:23.413
I understand why you believe that,

01:11:24.700 --> 01:11:27.150
but I find this to be pretty
ironic for a number of reasons.

01:11:27.150 --> 01:11:27.983
So,

01:11:29.220 --> 01:11:30.207
first thing is,

01:11:30.207 --> 01:11:33.230
this is a very effective strategy

01:11:33.230 --> 01:11:34.580
for people who are deconstructing,

01:11:34.580 --> 01:11:37.060
or people who are thinking
about deconstructing.

01:11:37.060 --> 01:11:38.480
Because in my experience,

01:11:38.480 --> 01:11:41.620
deconstructing people
tend to be very thoughtful

01:11:41.620 --> 01:11:44.020
and questioning of themselves.

01:11:44.020 --> 01:11:46.932
I had this exact same concern for years.

01:11:46.932 --> 01:11:49.210
But I find that most
deconstructing Christians

01:11:49.210 --> 01:11:51.930
have a lot of doubt in
their own reasoning,

01:11:51.930 --> 01:11:54.350
and that's precisely what
led them to where they are.

01:11:54.350 --> 01:11:57.100
They began to take a critical look,

01:11:57.100 --> 01:11:58.450
not simply at Christianity itself,

01:11:58.450 --> 01:12:00.370
but also to their adherence to it.

01:12:00.370 --> 01:12:01.203
So in other words,

01:12:01.203 --> 01:12:03.540
the deconstruction process
began as self doubt,

01:12:03.540 --> 01:12:05.300
or at least that was a part of it.

01:12:05.300 --> 01:12:09.010
So when you begin to
think, I remember writing,

01:12:09.010 --> 01:12:11.100
and I talked about this in
my deconstruction story.

01:12:11.100 --> 01:12:12.659
I specifically wrote that I did not

01:12:12.659 --> 01:12:14.770
just want to become my own God.

01:12:14.770 --> 01:12:16.840
I did not want to replace,

01:12:16.840 --> 01:12:18.890
I didn't wanna make God in my own image.

01:12:18.890 --> 01:12:21.350
I didn't wanna make a God
that I was comfortable with.

01:12:21.350 --> 01:12:24.950
Deconstructing people are
very conscious of this,

01:12:24.950 --> 01:12:26.110
and that's why when you tap into that,

01:12:26.110 --> 01:12:28.670
it is a very effective strategy

01:12:28.670 --> 01:12:30.190
to get them to come back into the fold,

01:12:30.190 --> 01:12:33.220
because they're very conscious
of being self-centered

01:12:33.220 --> 01:12:35.620
and relying on their own instincts,

01:12:35.620 --> 01:12:37.760
because that's the thing
that they begin questioning

01:12:37.760 --> 01:12:39.890
that even begins the
process to begin with.

01:12:39.890 --> 01:12:42.743
Yeah, and you know what
that effective strategy is?

01:12:44.700 --> 01:12:45.800
Shame.

01:12:45.800 --> 01:12:48.020
It's one word, it is shame.

01:12:48.020 --> 01:12:48.853
Yeah.

01:12:48.853 --> 01:12:50.700
Slathered on.

01:12:50.700 --> 01:12:52.000
Yeah, I agree with that.

01:12:53.770 --> 01:12:57.190
But maybe, this is a
little bit more dismissive.

01:12:57.190 --> 01:13:00.129
I don't disagree with it.

01:13:00.129 --> 01:13:00.962
No, no,
no.

01:13:00.962 --> 01:13:01.795
I feel it.

01:13:01.795 --> 01:13:04.770
I completely agree, I'm
moving to the next point.

01:13:04.770 --> 01:13:05.603
I'll talk about it more next week.

01:13:05.603 --> 01:13:06.730
My other issue with this is it

01:13:06.730 --> 01:13:08.730
assumes that the non-deconstructing

01:13:08.730 --> 01:13:10.870
Christian is the more selfless person.

01:13:10.870 --> 01:13:11.807
Right?

01:13:11.807 --> 01:13:13.780
That they are not following
their own instincts,

01:13:13.780 --> 01:13:16.643
but rather submitting
to and following God.

01:13:18.150 --> 01:13:20.170
Now, as someone who doesn't,

01:13:20.170 --> 01:13:22.540
who no longer believes that
that's how the world works,

01:13:22.540 --> 01:13:25.630
and I don't actually believe
that you as a Christian

01:13:25.630 --> 01:13:28.920
have the spirit of God in
you in a way that I don't,

01:13:28.920 --> 01:13:32.140
and you have discernment
from him that I don't.

01:13:32.140 --> 01:13:34.370
I actually think that we're
both doing the same thing,

01:13:34.370 --> 01:13:35.980
which could be characterized as selfish,

01:13:35.980 --> 01:13:37.290
if that's the word you want to use for it,

01:13:37.290 --> 01:13:40.820
and that is we, as a
product of our environment,

01:13:40.820 --> 01:13:43.483
our circumstances, and our genetics,

01:13:44.800 --> 01:13:46.350
all factors.

01:13:46.350 --> 01:13:49.130
We are making a decision about pretty much

01:13:49.130 --> 01:13:51.610
everything that we think
is the best for us, right?

01:13:51.610 --> 01:13:53.490
That's what humans do.

01:13:53.490 --> 01:13:55.540
We take all the information that we have,

01:13:56.380 --> 01:13:57.970
and all the instincts that we have,

01:13:57.970 --> 01:13:59.630
and we just make a decision that

01:13:59.630 --> 01:14:01.380
we feel is best for us at the time.

01:14:02.460 --> 01:14:03.820
Now, Christians,

01:14:03.820 --> 01:14:06.680
and specifically the
guys who wrote this book,

01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:09.050
are basically farming that out,

01:14:09.050 --> 01:14:11.120
which I believe is a
decision that they've made

01:14:11.120 --> 01:14:12.980
to make a decision to
say that they believe

01:14:12.980 --> 01:14:14.330
the Bible is an inherent word of God,

01:14:14.330 --> 01:14:15.250
that they're gonna be Christians,

01:14:15.250 --> 01:14:16.220
that this is what they're gonna believe,

01:14:16.220 --> 01:14:18.350
that they're gonna be
reformed, whatever it is.

01:14:18.350 --> 01:14:20.080
And then they're saying that this is God.

01:14:20.080 --> 01:14:21.198
This is me submitting to God.

01:14:21.198 --> 01:14:24.070
It's sort of a Jedi mind
trick of farming out

01:14:24.070 --> 01:14:27.530
their own choices to
an entity that is God.

01:14:27.530 --> 01:14:29.240
That's how I see that, right?

01:14:29.240 --> 01:14:30.710
I think I'm doing the same thing,

01:14:30.710 --> 01:14:31.730
I'm just not farming it out.

01:14:31.730 --> 01:14:32.580
I am saying, yeah,

01:14:32.580 --> 01:14:34.070
I am making this decision.

01:14:34.070 --> 01:14:35.430
And I know that a lot of this may not

01:14:35.430 --> 01:14:37.210
even be decisions that
I have control over,

01:14:37.210 --> 01:14:39.620
because I don't even know
how I feel about free will,

01:14:39.620 --> 01:14:41.010
and determinism, and all that stuff.

01:14:41.010 --> 01:14:43.510
You know, am I just a subject,

01:14:43.510 --> 01:14:45.490
a victim of my own
circumstances and genetics?

01:14:45.490 --> 01:14:46.323
I don't know, maybe,

01:14:46.323 --> 01:14:47.730
but it doesn't feel that way.

01:14:49.750 --> 01:14:51.970
So I take issue with that fundamentally,

01:14:51.970 --> 01:14:53.300
that they are somehow different.

01:14:53.300 --> 01:14:55.230
But also, again,

01:14:55.230 --> 01:14:59.420
it's sort of broadly categorizing
people who deconstruct

01:14:59.420 --> 01:15:03.163
as people who are selfish
and self centered.

01:15:04.462 --> 01:15:05.640
That's the implication.

01:15:05.640 --> 01:15:07.840
It's also kind of just
explicitly said here,

01:15:09.154 --> 01:15:11.913
but the most interesting
thing about this, to me,

01:15:13.830 --> 01:15:17.910
is that for me personally,

01:15:17.910 --> 01:15:20.640
the thing that was the
most difficult process,

01:15:20.640 --> 01:15:23.560
a difficult element of
my deconstruction process

01:15:23.560 --> 01:15:26.453
was the de-centering of myself.

01:15:27.530 --> 01:15:28.563
Let me explain that.

01:15:29.510 --> 01:15:34.020
De-centering myself from the
story of the universe, right?

01:15:34.020 --> 01:15:36.380
Now, this is an old story.

01:15:36.380 --> 01:15:38.240
This is how Christianity has interacted

01:15:38.240 --> 01:15:42.900
with new facts for a very long time,

01:15:42.900 --> 01:15:43.733
right?

01:15:43.733 --> 01:15:45.240
The Church is always the last people

01:15:45.240 --> 01:15:48.080
to get on board with unsettling facts

01:15:48.080 --> 01:15:50.203
that challenge their perspective.

01:15:51.390 --> 01:15:56.100
The heliocentric view of the world,

01:15:56.100 --> 01:15:58.660
meaning that the sun, or the
view of the solar system,

01:15:58.660 --> 01:16:01.680
meaning that the sun is the
center of our solar system,

01:16:01.680 --> 01:16:03.880
versus the geocentric view,

01:16:03.880 --> 01:16:05.720
which is that the Earth is in the middle

01:16:05.720 --> 01:16:06.970
and everything's rotating around it.

01:16:06.970 --> 01:16:09.410
Of course, for many generations,

01:16:09.410 --> 01:16:11.430
everyone believed that
the Earth was central,

01:16:11.430 --> 01:16:12.263
because we're like, of course,

01:16:12.263 --> 01:16:13.544
this is this what we see.

01:16:13.544 --> 01:16:14.980
This is from our perspective.

01:16:14.980 --> 01:16:16.200
We're the middle of this.

01:16:16.200 --> 01:16:18.600
That's what the Bible taught very clearly,

01:16:18.600 --> 01:16:21.950
and it's what the Church
believed for a really long time.

01:16:21.950 --> 01:16:23.210
And the reason that it took them

01:16:23.210 --> 01:16:25.090
hundreds of years to accept it,

01:16:25.090 --> 01:16:27.730
and people were killed because of this,

01:16:27.730 --> 01:16:29.700
is fundamentally because it's

01:16:29.700 --> 01:16:33.130
taking humans off of the center,

01:16:33.130 --> 01:16:35.280
off of the throne of the universe.

01:16:35.280 --> 01:16:36.420
And it's saying, no,

01:16:36.420 --> 01:16:37.253
no, no.

01:16:37.253 --> 01:16:39.330
You're not as special
as you thought you were.

01:16:39.330 --> 01:16:43.230
You might just be a lucky branch

01:16:43.230 --> 01:16:44.840
on the evolutionary tree, right?

01:16:44.840 --> 01:16:47.070
Because that's the second
piece of it, is evolution,

01:16:47.070 --> 01:16:50.250
which the church has
still not accepted, right?

01:16:50.250 --> 01:16:53.100
Some Christians do believe it, right?

01:16:53.100 --> 01:16:54.980
And to me this is so significant

01:16:54.980 --> 01:16:57.470
because believing in evolution was

01:16:57.470 --> 01:16:59.570
the first card to fall for me.

01:16:59.570 --> 01:17:00.403
Now, disclaimer,

01:17:00.403 --> 01:17:01.660
I know that there's lots of Christians

01:17:01.660 --> 01:17:04.110
who believe in evolution,

01:17:04.110 --> 01:17:05.700
however, most don't,

01:17:05.700 --> 01:17:07.433
and many of the ones that do,

01:17:09.540 --> 01:17:11.700
I don't really think have followed it

01:17:12.610 --> 01:17:14.297
to its logical conclusion
of what it actually means

01:17:14.297 --> 01:17:16.040
and how it relates to the creation story,

01:17:16.040 --> 01:17:16.873
that kind of thing.

01:17:16.873 --> 01:17:19.470
But, you know,

01:17:19.470 --> 01:17:23.735
this was so difficult for
me because, as a Christian,

01:17:23.735 --> 01:17:26.820
everything exists for you, right?

01:17:26.820 --> 01:17:27.940
Now, yes,

01:17:27.940 --> 01:17:29.200
and God, right?

01:17:29.200 --> 01:17:31.520
But God set you apart as special.

01:17:31.520 --> 01:17:32.880
You're not related to the animals.

01:17:32.880 --> 01:17:34.160
You're a special creation!

01:17:34.160 --> 01:17:36.750
The animals exist for your pleasure.

01:17:36.750 --> 01:17:37.640
God's pleasure, yeah,

01:17:37.640 --> 01:17:38.990
but your pleasure.

01:17:38.990 --> 01:17:42.020
I mean, that's what Genesis talks about.

01:17:42.020 --> 01:17:44.010
The Earth was made for Adam,

01:17:44.010 --> 01:17:45.740
and then, Adam,

01:17:45.740 --> 01:17:47.080
these animals are not good enough.

01:17:47.080 --> 01:17:49.390
Let me give you one that you
can actually have sex with.

01:17:49.390 --> 01:17:50.540
Here's a woman.

01:17:50.540 --> 01:17:51.855
You know?

01:17:51.855 --> 01:17:54.180
And so all these things are created

01:17:54.180 --> 01:17:56.310
so you can have dominion over them.

01:17:56.310 --> 01:17:57.490
And then everything that,

01:17:57.490 --> 01:18:00.570
the entire sort of ancient New Eastern

01:18:00.570 --> 01:18:02.250
view of the world and the cosmos,

01:18:02.250 --> 01:18:03.580
of it being very, very small,

01:18:03.580 --> 01:18:07.077
and it being this disc of an
Earth with a dome over it,

01:18:07.077 --> 01:18:09.000
and the water's below,
and the water's above,

01:18:09.000 --> 01:18:10.450
and the firmament in between.

01:18:11.320 --> 01:18:14.510
It brought everything
down and very, very close.

01:18:14.510 --> 01:18:15.550
They looked at the dome,

01:18:15.550 --> 01:18:16.707
and they saw the stars hanging from it,

01:18:16.707 --> 01:18:18.110
and it was just, I don't know,

01:18:18.110 --> 01:18:20.516
that's just right up there.

01:18:20.516 --> 01:18:21.708
If I had a,

01:18:21.708 --> 01:18:23.470
if I was strong enough, I
could throw a rock and hit it.

01:18:23.470 --> 01:18:24.303
You know what I'm saying?

01:18:24.303 --> 01:18:26.890
It was small and you were big.

01:18:26.890 --> 01:18:31.890
And with every successive
scientific revelation,

01:18:32.160 --> 01:18:34.030
we get smaller, and smaller,

01:18:34.030 --> 01:18:36.130
and more insignificant
in the scheme of things,

01:18:36.130 --> 01:18:39.373
and that is very uncomfortable
for a Christian mindset.

01:18:40.350 --> 01:18:41.520
You know, Christians,

01:18:41.520 --> 01:18:43.840
many Christians don't wanna believe,

01:18:43.840 --> 01:18:46.620
are very resistant to the idea of aliens.

01:18:46.620 --> 01:18:50.800
Not because we haven't
necessarily seen any,

01:18:50.800 --> 01:18:53.220
which is the reason that I
don't know if they exist,

01:18:53.220 --> 01:18:55.560
but because what does
that mean about Jesus?

01:18:55.560 --> 01:18:56.830
So they have another Jesus?

01:18:56.830 --> 01:18:57.810
Did Jesus go to them?

01:18:57.810 --> 01:18:58.940
Is that the other sheep that they're

01:18:58.940 --> 01:19:00.380
talking about in the Bible?

01:19:00.380 --> 01:19:01.213
I have other sheep.

01:19:01.213 --> 01:19:02.537
Well, it must be aliens.

01:19:02.537 --> 01:19:03.370
You know?

01:19:04.340 --> 01:19:05.940
You gotta fit it into your worldview.

01:19:05.940 --> 01:19:08.610
So I think what I'm saying is that

01:19:09.470 --> 01:19:12.380
the traditional Christian
perspective is actually

01:19:12.380 --> 01:19:15.410
more self-centered than a
perspective that sees humans

01:19:15.410 --> 01:19:17.293
as another part of the universe.

01:19:18.500 --> 01:19:20.570
Now I'm not talking about individuals.

01:19:20.570 --> 01:19:22.010
I'm not saying that Christians are

01:19:22.010 --> 01:19:23.510
more selfish than non-Christians.

01:19:23.510 --> 01:19:24.690
I'm not saying that non-Christians

01:19:24.690 --> 01:19:26.130
are more selfish than Christians.

01:19:26.130 --> 01:19:29.880
I think that your level
of selfishness is largely

01:19:29.880 --> 01:19:32.450
unrelated to your religious
convictions and conclusions.

01:19:32.450 --> 01:19:36.350
There's a lot of selfish inside
and outside of the Church,

01:19:36.350 --> 01:19:37.530
and there's lots of reasons that

01:19:37.530 --> 01:19:39.300
contribute to people being selfish,

01:19:39.300 --> 01:19:40.260
right?

01:19:40.260 --> 01:19:43.620
But I'm saying that the
philosophy of Christianity

01:19:43.620 --> 01:19:46.460
is a more human centered philosophy

01:19:46.460 --> 01:19:48.530
than a naturalistic worldview.

01:19:48.530 --> 01:19:51.040
The naturalistic worldview
puts you in concert,

01:19:51.040 --> 01:19:53.090
puts you in connection, interconnection,

01:19:53.090 --> 01:19:54.140
with everything else.

01:19:55.050 --> 01:19:56.750
There was a big bang at the beginning,

01:19:56.750 --> 01:19:59.030
and matter has organized itself,

01:19:59.030 --> 01:20:01.320
or was organized by
some entity that I can't

01:20:01.320 --> 01:20:04.010
really identify into what it is now,

01:20:04.010 --> 01:20:06.540
but we are star dust,
and so is the elephant.

01:20:06.540 --> 01:20:08.500
And the earth isn't really any more

01:20:08.500 --> 01:20:10.600
mine than it is the elephants, right?

01:20:10.600 --> 01:20:12.640
And just because I'm smarter,

01:20:12.640 --> 01:20:13.473
and just because I have more

01:20:13.473 --> 01:20:14.780
self-awareness than the elephant,

01:20:14.780 --> 01:20:16.210
I should be able to do whatever I want to?

01:20:16.210 --> 01:20:17.043
No!

01:20:18.410 --> 01:20:23.410
So the philosophy is more selfish,

01:20:24.220 --> 01:20:27.050
and it just feels like
there's a complete failure

01:20:27.050 --> 01:20:31.010
to see that in this
accusation that the person

01:20:31.010 --> 01:20:32.610
who begins to break away from that

01:20:32.610 --> 01:20:35.600
traditional Orthodox
way of seeing the world,

01:20:35.600 --> 01:20:38.930
Christian way of seeing the
world, is somehow selfish.

01:20:38.930 --> 01:20:39.763
And I'm like,

01:20:39.763 --> 01:20:40.596
hey, man.

01:20:40.596 --> 01:20:43.230
The most difficult part
of this process for me

01:20:43.230 --> 01:20:48.053
was realizing that I wasn't
as special as I thought I was.

01:20:49.730 --> 01:20:50.563
So it kind of,

01:20:50.563 --> 01:20:55.560
so that specific accusation
rings very, very hollow to me,

01:20:55.560 --> 01:20:58.173
and is pretty dismissive, you know,

01:20:59.550 --> 01:21:00.383
along the way.

01:21:02.350 --> 01:21:05.450
But I wanna bring it back.

01:21:05.450 --> 01:21:06.690
Bring it back.

01:21:06.690 --> 01:21:09.483
To what I was talking about earlier,

01:21:10.950 --> 01:21:15.950
and that is this idea that
leaning into uncomfortable truths

01:21:17.150 --> 01:21:21.190
rather than recoiling from them
is always more illuminating,

01:21:21.190 --> 01:21:23.510
and ultimately more spiritual.

01:21:23.510 --> 01:21:26.483
And I want to use evolution
as an example again.

01:21:29.870 --> 01:21:31.520
You know, when I was a Christian,

01:21:32.888 --> 01:21:35.373
and before I started
believing in evolution,

01:21:36.410 --> 01:21:39.520
I saw evolution as first
a desperate attempt

01:21:39.520 --> 01:21:42.107
to explain the universe
apart from God, right?

01:21:42.107 --> 01:21:43.040
It was like, you gotta
come up with something,

01:21:43.040 --> 01:21:45.430
so maybe they just happened spontaneously,

01:21:45.430 --> 01:21:46.410
and everything's related, and,

01:21:46.410 --> 01:21:47.243
well, I don't know.

01:21:47.243 --> 01:21:48.100
Making stuff up, right?

01:21:50.540 --> 01:21:52.930
I also saw it as a direct threat

01:21:52.930 --> 01:21:55.530
to the way that I understood the world.

01:21:55.530 --> 01:21:57.480
I saw it as a direct threat in terms

01:21:57.480 --> 01:21:59.040
of the veracity of scripture,

01:21:59.040 --> 01:22:00.570
but also a direct threat in terms

01:22:00.570 --> 01:22:02.890
of my place in the universe,

01:22:02.890 --> 01:22:04.850
as this is for me.

01:22:04.850 --> 01:22:06.090
The world is about, you know,

01:22:06.090 --> 01:22:08.460
God created humans to be
in relationship with him,

01:22:08.460 --> 01:22:11.543
and everything else that
is under that is for us.

01:22:14.860 --> 01:22:16.660
And I, first of all,

01:22:16.660 --> 01:22:17.810
I never really understood it.

01:22:17.810 --> 01:22:20.430
I never honestly considered it, right?

01:22:20.430 --> 01:22:23.090
And then when I finally
did honestly consider it,

01:22:23.090 --> 01:22:25.080
it was the first card.

01:22:25.080 --> 01:22:26.693
Everything began to fall apart.

01:22:27.800 --> 01:22:32.090
But on the other side of it, that truth,

01:22:32.090 --> 01:22:35.360
that truth of the
interconnectedness of all things,

01:22:35.360 --> 01:22:37.850
of every single thing
that I can touch and see

01:22:37.850 --> 01:22:39.800
in the world literally
being related to me,

01:22:39.800 --> 01:22:43.860
every animal that I can see
literally being my cousin,

01:22:43.860 --> 01:22:45.383
that's a life changing truth.

01:22:46.840 --> 01:22:49.580
That's a life changing truth.

01:22:49.580 --> 01:22:52.000
That sense of interconnectedness changes

01:22:52.000 --> 01:22:54.380
the way that you interact
with other people.

01:22:54.380 --> 01:22:57.600
It changes the way that you
interact with the environment,

01:22:57.600 --> 01:22:58.443
the world.

01:22:59.380 --> 01:23:01.230
It changes the way you see yourself.

01:23:01.230 --> 01:23:03.600
It changes the way that you see

01:23:03.600 --> 01:23:07.210
the responsibility that
we have to maintain

01:23:07.210 --> 01:23:08.420
this whole thing that we've got going,

01:23:08.420 --> 01:23:11.730
and the fragility of it, right?

01:23:11.730 --> 01:23:12.563
So.

01:23:14.610 --> 01:23:16.423
I think what I'm saying is that,

01:23:17.470 --> 01:23:18.313
you were saying,

01:23:20.702 --> 01:23:22.390
what is this leaning into the truth?

01:23:22.390 --> 01:23:24.663
Are you leaning into
the truth for meaning?

01:23:25.520 --> 01:23:29.190
What I'm saying is that
leaning into the truth,

01:23:29.190 --> 01:23:30.853
for whatever reason,

01:23:33.330 --> 01:23:35.780
there's going to be meaning
that comes from that.

01:23:36.970 --> 01:23:39.290
Especially if that's
just your disposition,

01:23:39.290 --> 01:23:41.150
is to find meaning in things, right?

01:23:41.150 --> 01:23:43.840
We're meaning makers, we can't help it.

01:23:43.840 --> 01:23:46.390
From the very beginning
of our consciousness,

01:23:46.390 --> 01:23:47.380
we've had this,

01:23:47.380 --> 01:23:49.420
we went from thinking that there was

01:23:50.740 --> 01:23:53.340
something moving in the bushes to,

01:23:53.340 --> 01:23:55.563
you know, ascribing agency to things.

01:23:56.619 --> 01:23:57.680
We were like, okay,

01:23:57.680 --> 01:23:58.963
it didn't rain today.

01:24:00.190 --> 01:24:02.660
Well, God must be upset with us.

01:24:02.660 --> 01:24:03.703
Let's dance.

01:24:04.816 --> 01:24:05.770
Let's pray.

01:24:05.770 --> 01:24:06.603
Oh, it rained.

01:24:06.603 --> 01:24:07.720
It must have been because we danced.

01:24:07.720 --> 01:24:09.880
It must have been because we prayed.

01:24:09.880 --> 01:24:12.110
This is what we do, we can't help it.

01:24:12.110 --> 01:24:14.800
We can't help but be meaning makers.

01:24:14.800 --> 01:24:18.210
It's in our blood, it's in our DNA.

01:24:18.210 --> 01:24:19.790
It's who we are.

01:24:19.790 --> 01:24:24.790
And so what I'm saying is
that I want to learn more,

01:24:24.860 --> 01:24:27.590
and lean more into truth,

01:24:27.590 --> 01:24:29.920
and not because I'm looking for meaning,

01:24:29.920 --> 01:24:32.080
but because truth is
interesting to me, right?

01:24:32.080 --> 01:24:33.940
Knowing more about something,

01:24:33.940 --> 01:24:36.060
and having it more accurately described,

01:24:36.060 --> 01:24:38.470
and not being scared of where it's leading

01:24:38.470 --> 01:24:40.260
has only been a positive thing for me.

01:24:40.260 --> 01:24:43.920
And I use that, finally
accepting evolution,

01:24:43.920 --> 01:24:44.850
and then being like, okay,

01:24:44.850 --> 01:24:45.800
well, what's next?

01:24:45.800 --> 01:24:47.520
My whole process of deconstruction

01:24:47.520 --> 01:24:49.290
was kind of like a card would fall,

01:24:49.290 --> 01:24:51.130
and I would be like, oh shit.

01:24:51.130 --> 01:24:52.540
And I'd be like, okay.

01:24:52.540 --> 01:24:53.373
Well, God,

01:24:53.373 --> 01:24:54.510
you're in control.

01:24:54.510 --> 01:24:56.200
You have the power to
stop this at any point,

01:24:56.200 --> 01:24:58.170
but I'm gonna turn over
the other card, you know?

01:24:58.170 --> 01:25:00.610
And I would just keep
going and keep going.

01:25:00.610 --> 01:25:02.090
On the back end of that,

01:25:02.090 --> 01:25:05.970
what I found is that the
process of deconstructing

01:25:05.970 --> 01:25:07.910
and the truth that I now hold to

01:25:08.758 --> 01:25:11.690
have been some of the most
beautiful and life altering.

01:25:11.690 --> 01:25:14.440
Are they as orienting as Christianity was?

01:25:14.440 --> 01:25:16.430
No, they're not as orienting.

01:25:16.430 --> 01:25:18.730
Because that's what a
religious system does,

01:25:18.730 --> 01:25:20.180
is it orients your thinking,

01:25:20.180 --> 01:25:21.920
and it systematizes your thinking in a way

01:25:21.920 --> 01:25:24.440
that brings a certain level
of comfort and control.

01:25:24.440 --> 01:25:26.000
You don't get that when you step

01:25:26.000 --> 01:25:27.660
outside of a religious framework.

01:25:27.660 --> 01:25:30.070
I'm very willing to admit that.

01:25:30.070 --> 01:25:35.070
But again, being on that bridge
between hope and cynicism,

01:25:37.130 --> 01:25:40.720
I think that's where the meaning happens.

01:25:40.720 --> 01:25:42.540
And now, whereas,

01:25:42.540 --> 01:25:43.630
'cause, yeah,

01:25:43.630 --> 01:25:47.320
I've accepted the
interconnectedness of all things.

01:25:47.320 --> 01:25:49.705
I've accepted that I am a, you know,

01:25:49.705 --> 01:25:53.370
I am a lucky branch on
the evolutionary tree.

01:25:53.370 --> 01:25:54.460
Couple of things could have gone

01:25:54.460 --> 01:25:55.800
a little bit differently and we could be

01:25:55.800 --> 01:25:58.423
a couple of neanderthals
sitting here talking, right?

01:25:59.450 --> 01:26:02.190
It was a matter of circumstance,

01:26:02.190 --> 01:26:03.960
and that's okay!

01:26:03.960 --> 01:26:05.350
That doesn't make you,

01:26:05.350 --> 01:26:07.340
that actually makes, in my mind,

01:26:07.340 --> 01:26:09.090
that makes this even more significant.

01:26:09.090 --> 01:26:10.600
I'm like, well damn!

01:26:10.600 --> 01:26:13.180
It's like, we got to this point?

01:26:13.180 --> 01:26:14.380
Like, we're here?

01:26:14.380 --> 01:26:17.040
At the end of all this crazy
shit that's been going on,

01:26:17.040 --> 01:26:19.130
we're here right now?

01:26:19.130 --> 01:26:21.060
Experiencing a life?

01:26:21.060 --> 01:26:23.580
Being able to consider it
and look back on on it?

01:26:23.580 --> 01:26:26.177
Like, that's significant,

01:26:26.177 --> 01:26:28.840
and that is meaningful.

01:26:28.840 --> 01:26:31.220
And as it relates to the Bible,

01:26:31.220 --> 01:26:32.053
it's like, okay,

01:26:32.053 --> 01:26:33.210
well, hey,

01:26:33.210 --> 01:26:36.300
I'm not going at this
thinking that I've got to,

01:26:36.300 --> 01:26:38.160
maybe I'll find God in the letter,

01:26:38.160 --> 01:26:39.770
in the words of the Bible.

01:26:39.770 --> 01:26:40.603
Well, maybe I will.

01:26:40.603 --> 01:26:41.436
I'm not saying,

01:26:41.436 --> 01:26:45.020
I don't wanna be closed to either side.

01:26:45.020 --> 01:26:47.600
But what I'm saying is
that there's a whole

01:26:47.600 --> 01:26:50.530
layer of truth to the Bible that I

01:26:50.530 --> 01:26:54.000
never considered because
I was afraid of it.

01:26:54.000 --> 01:26:57.350
If you started talking about
critical about the Bible,

01:26:57.350 --> 01:26:58.990
it was so, and so I just,

01:26:58.990 --> 01:27:00.570
and then when I finally deconstructed,

01:27:00.570 --> 01:27:02.730
I was like, that stuff is triggering.

01:27:02.730 --> 01:27:04.280
I can't read the Bible
without getting triggered,

01:27:04.280 --> 01:27:05.130
and getting uncomfortable,

01:27:05.130 --> 01:27:06.330
so I'm just gonna put it on the shelf

01:27:06.330 --> 01:27:08.240
and not read it for a few years.

01:27:08.240 --> 01:27:09.410
And now I'm saying,

01:27:09.410 --> 01:27:10.950
no, I'm going back.

01:27:10.950 --> 01:27:11.783
And I'm saying,

01:27:11.783 --> 01:27:13.233
I'm not afraid of any,

01:27:14.160 --> 01:27:16.110
I'm just going, and
I'm just looking at it,

01:27:16.110 --> 01:27:19.010
and I'm looking at everything
you can know about it.

01:27:19.010 --> 01:27:23.097
And the truth is gonna appear, you know,

01:27:23.097 --> 01:27:25.260
and the meaning will come.

01:27:25.260 --> 01:27:26.570
I don't have to control it.

01:27:26.570 --> 01:27:30.593
I don't have to come in
with this preconceived idea.

01:27:32.140 --> 01:27:36.970
And last thing I'll say is
I understand that this is a,

01:27:36.970 --> 01:27:38.663
this whole process,
this whole conversation,

01:27:38.663 --> 01:27:42.175
it's an incredibly
privileged viewpoint, right?

01:27:42.175 --> 01:27:44.920
You know, that's one of the
things that you read about

01:27:44.920 --> 01:27:48.927
when you think about the Jewish
people who wrote the Bible,

01:27:48.927 --> 01:27:51.670
and what they were going through.

01:27:51.670 --> 01:27:54.324
They were going through a bunch of, man.

01:27:54.324 --> 01:27:56.270
And this is true of basically anybody

01:27:56.270 --> 01:27:59.200
who's put putting together
a religious tradition.

01:27:59.200 --> 01:28:01.480
It is usually out of necessity,

01:28:01.480 --> 01:28:04.080
and out of trying to somehow get

01:28:04.080 --> 01:28:07.580
through what they were going through.

01:28:07.580 --> 01:28:08.830
I mean, and also,

01:28:08.830 --> 01:28:12.400
you think about African
American spirituality, right?

01:28:12.400 --> 01:28:14.770
And you think about how there's this

01:28:14.770 --> 01:28:17.663
really ironic thing that happened where,

01:28:19.580 --> 01:28:23.440
you know, African slaves
took on the religion

01:28:23.440 --> 01:28:26.610
of their oppressors in
many different ways,

01:28:26.610 --> 01:28:29.003
and there's Black
Christian spirituality now,

01:28:30.500 --> 01:28:31.890
and they have a tradition,

01:28:31.890 --> 01:28:32.898
kind of all,

01:28:32.898 --> 01:28:35.720
and it actually talks a little
bit about this in this book,

01:28:35.720 --> 01:28:39.220
but a tradition of their own that,

01:28:39.220 --> 01:28:40.740
considering that and, like,

01:28:40.740 --> 01:28:42.450
sitting there and deconstructing that,

01:28:42.450 --> 01:28:46.420
that's a position of extreme
privilege for a couple of guys

01:28:46.420 --> 01:28:48.660
who are number four on
the Forbes money list.

01:28:48.660 --> 01:28:49.493
Yeah.

01:28:49.493 --> 01:28:50.830
Just under that nine year old.

01:28:50.830 --> 01:28:53.704
I have the ability to just sit here.

01:28:53.704 --> 01:28:55.800
I don't have hardship in my,

01:28:55.800 --> 01:28:58.190
and this is a philosophical
exercise for me.

01:28:58.190 --> 01:28:59.330
I recognize that.

01:28:59.330 --> 01:29:01.280
It's not one in which I'm going through

01:29:01.280 --> 01:29:04.490
this incredibly difficult
thing personally,

01:29:04.490 --> 01:29:07.333
where I'm crying out to God, right?

01:29:08.330 --> 01:29:12.870
Right now I live in such a
position of privilege and excess

01:29:12.870 --> 01:29:17.870
that I can explore these things
like a college professor.

01:29:18.460 --> 01:29:21.053
So I'm not saying that this is something

01:29:21.053 --> 01:29:23.630
that I am trying to apply to everybody,

01:29:23.630 --> 01:29:25.860
and everybody should do, like,

01:29:25.860 --> 01:29:28.460
some people are going through
something so difficult,

01:29:28.460 --> 01:29:30.780
and the way that they
see and understand Jesus

01:29:30.780 --> 01:29:33.140
has been indispensable for them.

01:29:33.140 --> 01:29:35.620
I'm not trying to take
that away from them.

01:29:35.620 --> 01:29:38.070
I'm not interested in
taking that away from them.

01:29:39.230 --> 01:29:40.063
You know,

01:29:40.063 --> 01:29:41.320
just like I'm not interested in taking,

01:29:41.320 --> 01:29:42.820
changing the minds of the Christians

01:29:42.820 --> 01:29:44.800
that I'm still friends with.

01:29:44.800 --> 01:29:46.470
They want to hear what I
have to say about that,

01:29:46.470 --> 01:29:48.400
or what I think about some
conclusion they come to,

01:29:48.400 --> 01:29:49.990
I'm happy to discuss it,

01:29:49.990 --> 01:29:54.990
but this isn't designed to
deconstruct other people's faith.

01:29:55.110 --> 01:29:58.900
I'm just saying, this is
how it happened for me,

01:29:58.900 --> 01:30:01.537
this is how it continues to happen for me.

01:30:01.537 --> 01:30:04.570
And I recognize that I'm
able to do this just simply

01:30:04.570 --> 01:30:08.093
because I'm in a very
specific privileged position.

01:30:09.160 --> 01:30:09.993
Yeah.

01:30:09.993 --> 01:30:10.826
I think people,

01:30:12.030 --> 01:30:16.240
some people may write
you off and say, okay,

01:30:16.240 --> 01:30:21.240
you're basically saying you
don't have any need for Jesus,

01:30:21.280 --> 01:30:22.720
like as a personal savior.

01:30:22.720 --> 01:30:26.710
So I don't expect Rhett to get anything

01:30:26.710 --> 01:30:28.620
from him going back to the Bible,

01:30:28.620 --> 01:30:30.610
especially that version of the Bible.

01:30:30.610 --> 01:30:31.780
But you know what?

01:30:31.780 --> 01:30:33.590
It's less about the version of the Bible,

01:30:33.590 --> 01:30:38.590
and more about what his needs are,

01:30:38.750 --> 01:30:41.090
and is he open to having those met,

01:30:41.090 --> 01:30:43.190
I think is the criticism that, you know,

01:30:43.190 --> 01:30:45.700
that's the story that people

01:30:45.700 --> 01:30:47.260
will tell from one vantage point.

01:30:47.260 --> 01:30:48.187
And I, and you know,

01:30:48.187 --> 01:30:50.510
and I'll go back to what I said before,

01:30:50.510 --> 01:30:53.793
with the accusation of this is
just a self-centered pursuit.

01:30:54.710 --> 01:30:57.750
I know for a fact that this conversation

01:30:57.750 --> 01:31:00.142
is only going to reinforce
that perspective,

01:31:00.142 --> 01:31:01.580
if that's what you think.

01:31:01.580 --> 01:31:05.070
My perspective is that
we're all doing that.

01:31:05.070 --> 01:31:09.580
We're all synthesizing and
making personal decisions,

01:31:09.580 --> 01:31:12.130
and there's lots of different factors.

01:31:12.130 --> 01:31:14.820
It's very complicated and it's very muddy,

01:31:14.820 --> 01:31:16.680
and I'm not gonna fault you for coming.

01:31:16.680 --> 01:31:17.590
And I have done that.

01:31:17.590 --> 01:31:20.040
I'll stand up and say I have
faulted people for coming.

01:31:20.040 --> 01:31:22.980
The thing I will say is if
you subscribe to a system

01:31:22.980 --> 01:31:26.720
or you actively are discriminating against

01:31:26.720 --> 01:31:29.950
or belittling marginalized people,

01:31:29.950 --> 01:31:32.920
I'm gonna stand up for those
marginalized people, right?

01:31:32.920 --> 01:31:35.470
That's one place that
I'm not gonna compromise,

01:31:35.470 --> 01:31:40.440
but when it comes to your personal choices

01:31:40.440 --> 01:31:42.271
about what you end up
thinking about the Bible,

01:31:42.271 --> 01:31:43.140
and what you think about Jesus,

01:31:43.140 --> 01:31:43.973
it's just like?

01:31:45.320 --> 01:31:49.040
I know that you can't
make someone believe.

01:31:49.040 --> 01:31:50.510
You can't make me believe something.

01:31:50.510 --> 01:31:52.030
I can't make you believe something.

01:31:52.030 --> 01:31:54.760
Beliefs are things that happen

01:31:54.760 --> 01:31:57.836
spontaneously based on circumstances.

01:31:58.700 --> 01:31:59.533
You know?

01:32:01.350 --> 01:32:02.183
Which,

01:32:03.870 --> 01:32:06.050
you know, I think is ironic in one sense,

01:32:06.050 --> 01:32:07.570
because this is all, you know,

01:32:07.570 --> 01:32:08.610
this whole thing is being written

01:32:08.610 --> 01:32:10.077
from the reform perspective,

01:32:10.077 --> 01:32:12.340
and the very first
introduction talks about

01:32:12.340 --> 01:32:13.820
the parable of the sower being

01:32:13.820 --> 01:32:16.680
a framework for understanding this.

01:32:16.680 --> 01:32:17.513
And it's just like,

01:32:17.513 --> 01:32:19.930
there's a part of me
that's just like, hey,

01:32:19.930 --> 01:32:21.480
if you really are reformed,

01:32:21.480 --> 01:32:23.020
and you believe that there are some people

01:32:23.020 --> 01:32:26.010
who are elected to be children of God,

01:32:26.010 --> 01:32:27.340
and some people who are not,

01:32:27.340 --> 01:32:30.160
by the way, the vast majority of people.

01:32:30.160 --> 01:32:32.653
Well, why write this book at all?

01:32:33.650 --> 01:32:35.942
Why not just say that in a tweet,

01:32:35.942 --> 01:32:37.242
you know?

01:32:38.780 --> 01:32:40.450
I digress.

01:32:40.450 --> 01:32:43.003
Well, and I'll share next week.

01:32:44.390 --> 01:32:46.290
Yeah, you've given me,

01:32:46.290 --> 01:32:48.153
there's a number of things
I wanna springboard off of--

01:32:48.153 --> 01:32:50.620
You gonna buy a Bible?

01:32:50.620 --> 01:32:52.530
If so, you should order it now.

01:32:52.530 --> 01:32:55.425
It's gonna take a month
and a half to get here.

01:32:55.425 --> 01:32:57.043
You can photocopy mine,

01:32:57.043 --> 01:32:58.490
but that will probably
take you a few weeks.

01:32:58.490 --> 01:32:59.630
I have a few.

01:32:59.630 --> 01:33:03.240
I have a few at home still, thank you.

01:33:03.240 --> 01:33:04.220
And thanks for sharing.

01:33:04.220 --> 01:33:06.130
I think this is good.

01:33:06.130 --> 01:33:07.440
You didn't, you know,

01:33:07.440 --> 01:33:10.050
you didn't give me enough answers to know

01:33:10.050 --> 01:33:12.810
what I'm gonna do with the
rest of my spiritual life.

01:33:12.810 --> 01:33:15.007
You know, 'cause all I do is
just whatever you tell me.

01:33:15.007 --> 01:33:16.545
That's what people say about me.

01:33:17.960 --> 01:33:19.290
Well, but here's the thing.

01:33:19.290 --> 01:33:21.660
I'm coming up with things that
I know you're not gonna do.

01:33:21.660 --> 01:33:23.120
That's true, that is true.

01:33:23.120 --> 01:33:24.100
You're not gonna read the Bible--

01:33:24.100 --> 01:33:27.167
I am not buying this Bible, I am not.

01:33:27.167 --> 01:33:28.410
So you're on your own now.

01:33:28.410 --> 01:33:29.243
Oh yeah.

01:33:29.243 --> 01:33:30.076
Yeah, I love it.

01:33:30.076 --> 01:33:34.220
My rec is Richard Holloway's
'Stories We Tell Ourselves'.

01:33:34.220 --> 01:33:35.470
Love this guy.

01:33:35.470 --> 01:33:37.160
Check out Marginalia as well.

01:33:37.160 --> 01:33:39.540
I think it's themarginalian.com,

01:33:39.540 --> 01:33:40.393
and listen.

01:33:42.110 --> 01:33:43.070
Read this book, you know?

01:33:43.070 --> 01:33:43.920
Send the Gospel Co,

01:33:43.920 --> 01:33:45.820
well, maybe find a way to steal some.

01:33:45.820 --> 01:33:46.812
No, I'm just kidding.

01:33:46.812 --> 01:33:48.530
I'm just kidding.

01:33:48.530 --> 01:33:51.020
I think that if you are,

01:33:51.020 --> 01:33:53.470
this before you lose your faith is sort of

01:33:53.470 --> 01:33:57.080
a fascinating study of the way
that the Evangelical Church

01:33:57.080 --> 01:34:00.260
is trying to process what's happening.

01:34:00.260 --> 01:34:02.270
And it's it, like I said,

01:34:02.270 --> 01:34:04.440
I think this is about the
best attempt that can be

01:34:04.440 --> 01:34:09.093
